/target
/target-coverage
# The MSRV check builds into its own directory for the same reason coverage
# does: a different toolchain invalidates the cache, so sharing one with the
# normal dev build means every MSRV run rebuilds the world twice over.
/target-msrv
# cargo-fuzz builds into its own directory, since fuzz/ is a separate workspace.
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/artifacts
/fuzz/coverage
# Seeded by crates/pgprox-proto/examples/seed_corpus.rs and then grown by
# libFuzzer into several thousand small files no human reads. The seeder is
# the committed part; what a run discovers from it is not.
/fuzz/corpus
**/*.rs.bk
.env
*.pem
*.key

# Scratch. Anything somebody needs to put somewhere and nobody needs to keep:
# the upstream proxies cloned for protocol reference, a profile, a working copy.
# One entry rather than one per artefact, and the place to put the next one.
/.tmp

# The rest of the scratch, which cannot go in there.
#
# Each of these is a tool that writes to the working directory and gives the
# repository no say in it. `perf record`, `cargo flamegraph`, `cargo mutants`,
# `cargo llvm-cov` and a dhat binary all default to CWD, so a hand-run from the
# repository root lands here whatever `/.tmp` says. Folding them in would mean
# the redirect had to be typed by the person running the command, which is the
# one place it will be forgotten.
#
# `M49` checked whether any of these is produced by a script in this repository,
# because a script can be told where to write. None is: `scripts/bench.sh` puts
# callgrind output in a mktemp directory, `scripts/mutants.sh` writes under
# `target/`, and `scripts/profile.sh` writes to `target/profile`. Every line
# below guards a manual run and nothing else.
*.profraw
*.profdata
/coverage
perf.data*
flamegraph.svg
callgrind.out.*
dhat-heap.json
/mutants.out
/mutants.out.old

# The documentation site, which is built from the pages beside it in `docs/`.
# These three are what that build downloads and produces, and they are the
# reason the collection's glob does not recurse: see docs/src/content.config.ts.
/docs/node_modules
/docs/dist
/docs/.astro
